# Network Branding — VTC Platform

Network admins configure branding in **Network settings** (shell → network profile → Branding policy). The platform does **not** hardcode private vs public behavior — defaults are suggested; the admin decides.

## Network settings (ZAPI `network_settings`)

| Field | Values | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| `branding_scope` | `network` \| `space` \| `hybrid` | Who controls accent color |
| `app_typography` | `platform` \| `network` | Child app font: VTC standard vs network font |
| `network_font` | See `NETWORK_FONT_IDS` in `@vtc/client` | Font when `app_typography=network` |

**`network_font` values:** `system`, `lato`, `inter`, `geist`, `manrope`, `plus-jakarta-sans`, `nunito-sans`, `poppins`, `dm-sans`, `atkinson-hyperlegible` (Google Fonts loaded on demand in child apps).
| `allow_space_theme_color` | boolean | Whether child spaces may set accent |

**Suggested defaults** (when unset — applied in shell `resolveNetworkBranding()`):

| Network type | `branding_scope` | `app_typography` | `network_font` | `allow_space_theme_color` |
|--------------|------------------|------------------|----------------|---------------------------|
| Private | `network` | `network` | `lato` | `false` |
| Public / open | `space` | `platform` | `system` | `true` |

## Accent scope

| Scope | Shell chrome | Child apps (`?color=`) |
|-------|--------------|------------------------|
| `network` | Network color only | Network color |
| `space` | Space color when set | Space color → network fallback |
| `hybrid` | Network color on rail | Space accent in apps; network in shell |

Shell: `syncShellBrandFromActiveSpace()` uses `isSpaceAccentAllowed()` — not hardcoded private-network checks.

## Child app URL params (shell → iframe)

Shell appends on every embed (`child-app-theme-params.ts`):

| Param | When | Child app |
|-------|------|-----------|
| `color` | Always (resolved from scope) | `--app-accent*` via `ThemeProvider` |
| `typography` | `platform` \| `network` | Font policy |
| `font` | When `typography=network` | Network font id → `--app-font-family` (see `@vtc/client` `NETWORK_FONT_IDS`) |
| `mode`, `lang` | As before | Dark/light, i18n |
| `tz` | User timezone preference (IANA) | Display times — `resolveUserTimeZone()` (`@vtc/client` ≥ 1.2.2) |

**Persist** with `preserveThemeParams()` / `addTokenToUrl()` from `@vtc/client` (v1.2.2+ for `tz` / `posif_tz`).

## Child apps — implementation

1. **`@vtc/client`** — `preserveThemeParams`, `addTokenToUrl`, `resolveAppFontFamily`, `NETWORK_FONT_STACKS`
2. **`src/lib/themeFonts.ts`** — `applyAppTypographyToDocument()` (loads Google Font when needed via `getNetworkFontGoogleHref`)
3. **`ThemeProvider`** — accepts `typography` + `font`; sets accent + font on `<html>`
4. **`globals.css`** — `@theme { --font-sans: var(--app-font-family, …) }` and `body { @apply font-sans }`

**Platform floor:** type **scale** (`text-sm`, `text-2xl`, etc.) stays per `ui.mdc` — only **font family** changes with network policy. Do not import ad-hoc fonts in components.

## Resolution order (accent — unchanged)

1. URL `color` (shell-injected)
2. `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ACCENT`
3. Persisted `posif_color`
4. VTC Blue `#004A80`

